   "he": "קָנָה שְׁלֹשָׁה – קָנָה קַרְקַע. וְכַמָּה? אָמַר רַבִּי חִיָּיא בַּר אַבָּא אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן: הֲרֵי זֶה קָנָה תַּחְתֵּיהֶן וּבֵינֵיהֶן, וְחוּצָה לָהֶן",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If «one bought three» trees «he has acquired» the «ground» along with them. The Gemara asks: «And how much» of the field does he acquire? «Rabbi Ḥiyya bar Abba says» that «Rabbi Yoḥanan says: This» buyer «has acquired» the ground that is located «underneath» the trees, «and» the area «between them, and» with regard to the space «outside of» the trees and their branches,"
